{"name":"Tap Shoe","hex":"#2f3032","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tap","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Taabwa."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A conical peg or pin used to close and open the hole or vent in a container.","An object with a tapering conical form like a tap (etymology 1, noun sense 1); specifically, ellipsis of taproot (“long, tapering root of a plant”).\n A hollow device used to control the flow of a fluid, such as an alcoholic beverage from a cask, or a gas or liquid in a pipe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap"},{"term":"shoe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A protective covering for the foot, with a bottom part composed of thick leather or plastic sole and often a thicker heel, and a softer upper part made of leather or synthetic material. Shoes generally do not extend above the ankle, as opposed to boots, which do.","A piece of metal designed to be attached to a horse's foot as a means of protection; a horseshoe."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put shoes on one's own feet.","To put shoes on someone or something else's feet, especially to put horseshoes on a horse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tap dance","blocks":[{"text":"Tap dance is a form of dance in which the dancers use sounds of tap shoes striking the floor as a form of percussion; it is often accompanied by music. Tap dancing can also be performed with no musical accompaniment; the sound of the taps is its own music."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Iowatapdancers.jpg/330px-Iowatapdancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tap_dance","wikidata":"Q244475"},{"title":"Shoe","blocks":[{"text":"A shoe is an item of footwear normally found in pairs intended to protect and comfort the human foot, usually made in such a way that 